# Deliberately empty. This file exists so `pnpm types` and `pnpm types:check` can point
# `wrangler types --env-file` at something that holds nothing (#132).
#
# Without it, `wrangler types` folds the keys of a developer's local `.dev.vars` into the
# generated `Env` — which false-fails `types:check` and, when they run `pnpm types` to
# "fix" it, writes their own secret names into the committed
# `src/worker-configuration.d.ts` as though they were part of the binding contract.
#
# `/dev/null` would do the same job and be empty by construction, but it does not exist
# on Windows, and `types:check` is the first step of `pnpm check` — a contributor there
# could not run the gate at all.
#
# **Never put a value in this file.** test/node/wrangler-types.test.ts parses it and
# fails if it defines anything, because a value here would silently become part of the
# generated types for everyone.
